    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier play (81.88). Facing Bailey Ober, **Henderson** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the starter's skill profile, combined with the optimizer's aggressive weighting toward his stolen base potential against Ober\u2019s slow delivery. We are also expecting significant production from **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.87) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45). **Robert Jr.** faces a favorable platoon advantage against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, while **Guerrero Jr.** is perfectly positioned in the three-hole to exploit a solid Park factor and a manageable matchup against Patrick Sandoval. **Kyle Tucker** (71.17) and **Jacob Wilson** (70.33) round out our high-efficiency core, both capitalizing on favorable SP xERA markers that elevate their baseline projections.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 47.78. While **Nunez** offers elite speed, his matchup against Shota Imanaga\u2014coupled with a lower-tier batting order projection and a specific penalty for Imanaga\u2019s ability to hold runners\u2014pushed him to the bench in favor of higher-floor assets. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (39.03) was never in serious contention, as the daunting xERA of Kyle Harrison combined with a brutal L/L platoon disadvantage severely handicapped his utility. All managers should remain alert to the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board; while we have modeled our scores based on historical batting orders, any significant displacement in the lineup for players like **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci** could necessitate a re-evaluation of their projected efficiency. We are currently avoiding any major weather-related risks, but the reliance on projected order positions remains our primary variable for risk management today.",
